Lab 19: Manage VM Security with SELinux and AppArmor
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Verify and interpret SELinux status and contexts as they apply to KubeVirt VM workloads
Create and load a custom AppArmor profile for VM launcher pods
Apply SELinux booleans and AppArmor annotations to a running virtual machine
Audit and troubleshoot SELinux denials and AppArmor enforcement events
Apply defensive security hardening practices for VM isolation on OpenShift Virtualization
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux mandatory access control concepts (SELinux and AppArmor)
Familiarity with OpenShift Container Platform fundamentals (pods, nodes, MachineConfig)
Knowledge of virtual machine concepts and KubeVirt (VirtualMachine, VirtualMachineInstance)
Experience with command-line interface operations
Understanding of YAML configuration files and basic oc CLI usage
This lab is performed entirely in an isolated, self-owned practice environment for defensive security training. No steps here weaken production security controls; every technique is used to observe, verify, and strengthen access control enforcement.

